From 39c5fefc727114e1d84d2729a80cfa4f881e4df1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Your Name <jonathan.ming.jun.lui@intel.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 19:21:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 122/122] script: acpi: mc-setup: add range syntax, native
 defaults, ar0234 guard

Add inclusive des=/link= range syntax (e.g. des=0-1,link=0-3) that
expands one CLI argument into every (des,link) combination, and allow
link= to be omitted entirely to mean every discovered link, optionally
scoped by des=, so a single res= argument can reconfigure every sensor.

Change the default resolution/format behaviour: an omitted or
unsupported res= now falls back to the sensor's native (largest)
advertised resolution instead of silently retaining whatever happened
to be active, and any discovered link left unmentioned by the CLI is
still programmed with its default stream and native settings so a
partial command never leaves other links in a stale state.

Reject stream=/format=/fps= on ar0234, which only supports des=,
link= and res=, printing a warning and ignoring those tokens instead
of silently applying them.

Add a --help/-h flag documenting the full CLI syntax, range
expansion, environment variable overrides and examples.

The patch no longer applied cleanly against this checkout of main,
which already carries the independently-added mipi= direct-MIPI
camera selector. Resolved by keeping mipi_sel alongside the new
range-expansion loop, and made expand_arg_ranges() pass mipi=N
arguments through unexpanded since they select a single camera
rather than a des=/link= range.

Signed-off-by: Goh, Wei Khang1 <wei.khang1.goh@intel.com>
---
 script/acpi/mc-setup.sh | 201 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
